        "by": "human",
        "reason": "[replay:data_rebuild] The MIMIC-on-FHIR warehouse was rebuilt on 2026-08-24 after two upstream data defects were fixed: FHIR resources are now generated under UTC, so wall-clock timestamps are no longer shifted an hour across the spring-forward boundary, and Patient.birthDate is now derived from the anchor year and age rather than from the first transfer. This port was carried forward byte-identical to re-measure it against the corrected data -- do not re-author it. Expect previously accepted divergences to have shrunk or gone; if an hour-wide shift still appears, treat it as a finding and establish why the correction did not reach that path rather than accepting it as an upstream artifact.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Judge accept: full schema and row counts match (193260 each); all 193260 events close under stay_id plus replayed effective endpoints, with 191421/193260 representable rows identical and zero unexplained residual after full-source replay. The 46 direct timestamp conflicts are the upstream America/New_York DST TIMESTAMPTZ transformation in mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_administration_icu.sql:8-9,61-69; the remaining apparent timing/amount conflicts are unkeyed stay-only pairing amplification from that timing loss and six-decimal Quantity serialization at mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_administration_icu.sql:12,85-90 and :14,91-99, whose original values are unrecoverable by FHIR query. linkorderid is declared all-NULL because the ICU ETL omits it at :7-23,38-100 and resource identity is opaque; it is ancillary administrative linkage. The single mcg/min vaso_rate NULL is the honest row-level consequence of omitted patientweight while rate unit survives at :91-99; it does not alter inclusion, grain, grouping, or carry-forward. Proven DST loss is not essential-loss blocking under the contract.",
